# Runs ONLY in the -O2 test runs (test-*-O2). This test exists to justify the
# `#pragma GCC optimize("no-reorder-blocks-and-partition")` that --backtraces
# emits: it only bites at -O2, where gcc hot/cold-splits functions. `probe`'s
# bounds-check failure block is cold and holds the non-tail call into the
# backtrace helper; with the split suppressed, probe's frame is correctly named.
# Remove the pragma and gcc -O2 drops `probe` (shows only `main`) — this test
# then fails. At -O0 there is no split, so running it there proves nothing.
# clang doesn't do this split by default and keeps `probe` regardless.
